{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/11","id":4885345349,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVLzC488AAAABIzB0RQ","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/11","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/11.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pull/11.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/11","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/11/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/11/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/issues/11/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/statuses/67f5366f452f1e56c4364026bfecd37f39c4dd41","number":11,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"test(os): reproduce unenforced Asterinas CPU cap; fix organ backend boundaries","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Scope and decision\nRetain Asterinas/OSTD as the concrete OS backend. Do not put ioctl/I/O/capabilities inside Hepta TrustedReadOnlyOrganV1; observation capture and effects remain under existing owners. No new kernel rewrite, HOS3, parallel authority or business ledger.\n\nBase main: `47afb8229bd3a3ff05077c7b01aac6fa8ef6f956`. HEAD: `67f5366f452f1e56c4364026bfecd37f39c4dd41`. 31 changed/new files, 293,335 bytes; remote blob hashes/sizes verified, README=0. Existing agent branches and main were not overwritten.\n\n## Actual execution\n- Independently replayed A01 #5 artifact at `b14e46105cd892f5e1186a46f1dcfc1ae270420a`: exact ELF/initramfs/SeaBIOS hashes; q35/TCG, 1 vCPU, 512MiB, no host networking or data disks; raw QEMU 33, CPU=1/BOOT_OK, no panic. This is artifact replay, NOT a source rebuild by this PR.\n- Added a statically compiled C Linux-ELF diagnostic and bounded in-memory initramfs runner. Inside the same unchanged Asterinas kernel, wrote/read back cpu.max=1000/100000 and verified process membership. Unlimited: CPU 997,000,000ns / wall 1,000,149,453ns. Configured 1%: CPU 998,000,000ns / wall 1,000,128,020ns, with the actual accepted-but-not-enforced warning. **Result NOT_ENFORCED, qualification_passed=false**. Runner exit0 means diagnostic completion, NOT a passing resource capability.\n- Preserved initial test-harness failure: Asterinas reports a Linux-compatible /proc/version; the first guard refused it. Fixed by pinned artifact hash in runner + disposable initramfs marker + Rust-built guest-version guard. No host cgroup changes; the compiled probe refuses the actual Linux host.\n- Archive safety tests: 5 pass normally and 5 pass under Python -O. Host refusal tested. Full logs and exact commands included.\n- Independently compiled A02 #4: original5 tests/release pass, strictClippy fails. Added two regression cases exposing final-legal-revision rejection. Separate stacked fix #10 provides Rust source and 7 passing tests/release/strictClippy/fmt. This PR contains its evidence, not duplicate codec source.\n\n## Files\n`tests/organ_backend/**`, `results/organ-backend/2026-10-16/**`, `docs/ASTERINAS_ORGAN_BACKEND.md`, narrow ARCHITECTURE/HEPTA_INTEGRATION additions and A05/A06/A07 prompt corrections.\n\n## Not completed\nNo CPU enforcement patch, memory-limit implementation, HOS2 kernel syscall, effectful Hepta organ integration, Android/GPU/bare-metal validation. This PR supplies the real failing guest regression and correct implementation boundary, not another completion claim. A00 can integrate without taking over A01/A02/A06 source ownership.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T08:02:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T08:39:12Z","closed_at":"2026-10-16T08:39:11Z","merged_at":"2026-10-16T08:39:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"c1a22de12f3d95fd49227787601169b9f42fdf12","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:agents/organ-backend-validation","ref":"agents/organ-backend-validation","repo":{"id":1421656803,"node_id":"R_kgDOVLzC4w","name":"trillionnium-os-desktop","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Trillion